tiled_scaling_2026-08-10 -- ATTRIBUTION of the tiled t=8 scaling deficit.
Narrative + verdict: docs/TILED_SCALING.md. This file is provenance only.

WHAT WAS MISSING BEFORE THIS
  The tiled scaling deficit had been measured three times (most recently
  benchmarks/size_sweep_t8_gap_2026-08-10) and profiled ZERO times. Every
  profile in the campaign's ~20 rounds was single-tile or t=1 -- the one shape
  where no tile parallelism exists -- so nothing that appears only when several
  tile workers and several superblock-row filter tasks are live at once could be
  seen at all.

HOST / BUILD
  Apple M4 Pro (Mac16,11, 8P+4E, 24 GB), macOS 26.5.2.
  rav1d-safe measure/tiled-t8-attribution, base main @ b700489, release,
  default features except where an arm names a probe feature.
  NO -C target-cpu=native. dav1d 1.5.4 (homebrew).
  MEASURE-ONLY: `git diff b700489..HEAD -- src/ lib.rs include/ crates/
  Cargo.toml Cargo.lock build.rs` is EMPTY. Only scripts/perf/, docs/ and
  benchmarks/ changed.

ARMS (all four are the same source tree; only cargo features differ)
  rs / bench_plain / ivf_plain   default features -- what ships
  untracked / ivf_untracked      + probe-untracked (borrow tracker compiled out)
  tt                             + probe-tasktime  (stage/worker/occupancy census)
  ttu                            + probe-tasktime-untracked
  dav1d_fd1                      dav1d --framedelay 1  (matched threading model:
                                 our checked build forces n_fc = 1, so frame
                                 threading is not an axis we have)
  dav1d_def                      dav1d default frame delay (frame threading ON;
                                 included to show what that axis is worth, NOT
                                 as the comparator)

  `untracked` is bit-identical to `rs`: tiled_md5_arms_2026-08-10.tsv, 8 of 8
  md5s equal over {plain, untracked} x {t=1, t=8} x both vectors.

VECTORS
  ~/tmp/t8gap/vec/L1024x576_420_8b__t8.avif   1024x576  YUV420 8bpc, 4x2 =  8 tiles,  9 sbrows
  ~/tmp/t8gap/vec/L3840x2160_420_8b__t8.avif  3840x2160 YUV420 8bpc, 4x2 =  8 tiles, 34 sbrows
  single-tile controls: L1024x576_420_8b.avif, L3840x2160_420_8b.avif
  IVF twins in ~/tmp/t8gap/ivf/ (same OBU replicated: 200 frames at 1024x576,
  16 at 4K -- `~/tmp/szsweep/mkivf.sh`). Provenance of the vectors themselves:
  benchmarks/size_sweep_t8_gap_2026-08-10.meta + ~/tmp/t8gap/enc_tiles.sh.

  ALL-INTRA. `bench_ab_decode` re-decodes one key-frame OBU, and the IVFs are
  that same OBU repeated, so there is no inter prediction and no reference
  management anywhere in this record. Loop restoration and super-resolution
  execute ZERO blocks on both vectors (0.000 ms/frame in every stage table) --
  a null from either here is not a result.

INSTRUMENTS
  1. src/probe_tasktime.rs via --features probe-tasktime: per-stage and
     per-worker busy ns, a 50 us time-weighted concurrency histogram, the
     tail-restricted histogram (no tile worker live, >=1 filter worker), and
     check_tile deferral causes. 2 Instant::now() per stage execution against
     ~45 stage executions/frame.
  2. /usr/bin/sample, 1 ms, 30 s windows, on the SHIPPING binary.
  3. bash `time` with TIMEFORMAT='%3R %3U %3S' (the child's getrusage), two
     frame counts per cell, `total = a + b*frames` fitted separately for wall
     and for user+sys so exec/mmap/decoder-construction/pool-spinup drop out.

  TWO INSTRUMENT TRAPS, both load-bearing for reading the tables:
  * At --threads 1 EVERY stage counter reads 0.000. n_tc == 1 creates no task
    worker, so rav1d_task_run -- where all the stage instrumentation lives -- is
    never entered. A per-stage t8/t1 ratio does not exist; the low arm is t=2 or
    t=4, which is also the better comparison (same code path as t=8:
    tile_threading_active() latched, narrow guards, adaptive block shift).
  * `sample` samples PARKED threads. __psynch_cvwait is 37.3% of leaves at t=8
    and 0.0% at t=1, so leaving it in the denominator deflates every busy
    symbol by exactly the amount the pool sleeps. Every percentage in
    tiled_selftime_* is normalised on BUSY samples, idle reported separately.

MEASUREMENT HYGIENE
  Every timed run under `measlock` (four separate holds: taskprobe, sample,
  wallcpu, inloop). Rotating arm order inside every cell. Medians with min/max
  bands printed per arm. Box essentially idle: foreign_max = 1 (taskprobe),
  2 (wallcpu, inloop). Builds were niced; timed runs never.

  ONE OUTLIER, NOT DROPPED: tiled_wallcpu_2026-08-10.tsv round 5, arm
  `untracked`, L3840x2160_420_8b__t8, t=1 reports wall_hi = 2000 ms where the
  other six rounds report 2996-3007, giving beta = 103.7 against a median of
  175.0. Cause not established. It is the `min` of that cell's band and does not
  move the median (6 of 7 rounds agree to 0.3%).

A HARNESS BUG FOUND AND FIXED MID-ROUND -- read this before reusing the script
  The first wallcpu pass used n_hi = 24 on the 4K cell. That IVF has 16 frames.
  `bench_plain` re-decodes one OBU exactly n times whatever you ask, but
  `dav1d --limit N` stops at end of stream -- so the two-point fit divided a
  SHORT total by a LONG frame delta and dav1d read 94.1 ms/frame instead of
  152.1 (a factor of 24/13 = 1.615x), which would have made dav1d look 1.96x
  faster than us single-threaded instead of 1.21x. Caught by comparing against
  the prior record's 156.071 and confirmed by counting the IVF's frames.
  scripts/perf/tiled_wallcpu.sh now counts every cell's stream and refuses
  n_hi > n_frames with a FATAL. All 4K rows in the committed TSV are from the
  re-run at 2:16. The 1024x576 cell was never affected (n_hi = 200 = the
  stream's exact length; verified linear: dav1d --limit {50,100,200} gives
  11.000 / 10.900 / 10.900 ms/frame).

